  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Aura</strong> faint Destruction; <strong>CL</strong> 2nd; <strong>SP</strong> 1<br>\n<strong>Slot</strong> none; <strong>Price</strong> 1,000 gp; <strong>Weight</strong> 2 lbs.<br>\n<strong>Damage</strong> 1d6 (2d6) nonlethal</p>\n<p>This slender wooden spell engine contains the Destruction sphere and the Gale Blast talent, as well as the Energy Focus (air) drawback. This spell engine is often given to apprentices to help them practice their magic and control; since it only deals nonlethal damage and can trip targets, it is frequently the weapon of choice in amateur spell duels. While it normally deals 1d6 nonlethal damage, the user can spend the single spell point it can hold to increase this damage to 2d6 nonlethal.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nCraft Spell Engine, Destruction sphere (Gale Blast (blast type)); <strong>Cost</strong> 500 gp</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/spell-engines#toc0\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
